1. Covered material

This license applies only to original enclosure designs, CAD source, CAD exports, code, preview
images and documentation in the Radar Camera Enclosure project that Chris Kalkowski (the "Licensor") has authority to license
(the "Covered Material"). It grants rights only to the extent the Licensor holds
those rights.

Texas Instruments software, firmware, SDKs, documentation, and other third-party
materials are excluded. Files or components with separate license notices remain
subject to their own licenses. This license does not replace those licenses or
grant rights in third-party materials.

2. Permitted use and modification

Subject to this license, you may use, copy, and modify the Covered Material for
personal use, teaching, and internal business use. Teaching may be paid or unpaid.
Individuals may use and modify the Covered Material for personal research.
Companies may use and modify it for internal research and as an internal tool
in their ordinary commercial activities. Earning income from activities in which the Covered
Material is used as a tool does not, by itself, violate this license.

3. Free redistribution

You may distribute the Covered Material and modified versions without charge,
provided that you retain this license and existing copyright and attribution
notices. You must clearly identify modified versions as modified. The permissions
and restrictions in this license continue to apply to the Covered Material in
those versions. You may not remove these restrictions by applying another license
to the Covered Material.

4. No resale or paid access

Without separate written permission from the applicable rights holder, you may
not:

(a) sell, rent, or commercially sublicense the Covered Material or modified
    versions;
(b) incorporate or distribute the Covered Material or modified versions as part
    of a product or bundle offered for payment, including a paid software product
    or a paid hardware-and-software bundle; or
(c) charge for access to the Covered Material or modified versions, including
    through a hosted service, subscription, premium version, or paid feature of
    another product or service.

The paid-teaching permission allows charging for instruction, including when
free copies are provided to students under section 3. It does not allow selling
the Covered Material, charging separately for copies or software access, or
offering paid software access as a product under the label of teaching.

These restrictions also apply to physical enclosures and components fabricated
from the Covered Material, including modified physical derivatives. Without
separate written permission, you may not independently manufacture them for
stock or inventory for sale, list or offer them for resale on a website or
elsewhere, or incorporate them into commercial products offered for sale.

Customer-directed fabrication exception: You may fabricate copies for your
own personal, teaching or internal business use as permitted by section 2.
You may hire a print shop or other fabricator to make those copies for you.
The fabricator may receive the necessary files and charge for that specific
customer-directed fabrication service, including its materials and labor,
and deliver the resulting copies to that customer. This exception applies
equally to modified physical derivatives. It does not authorize independent
stock manufacture, retail listings, resale or sale as commercial products,
or selling or charging for access to the design files themselves.

Independently created output merely produced using the Covered Material as a
tool is otherwise outside these restrictions; physical reproductions of these
enclosure designs are not such independent output.

Outputs and research rights: The Licensor claims no ownership, license,
revenue share or other rights in datasets, measurements, research findings,
trained models or independently created software merely because they were
produced while using this enclosure or radar. You may keep, use, share or sell
such independent outputs, subject to any independently applicable third-party
rights or laws. This does not permit sale of the enclosure CAD design, its
modified versions or physical enclosure copies. Contributions of datasets or
other outputs to the Licensor are entirely voluntary and separately opt-in.

